Time-out occurs when a client fails to bind to a server within
a time frame. When this time frame expires, the client re-attempt
to bind to the server. All this is done, transparently, in the
(client) stub code. I have experimented and observed the variability
of the time frame (i.e., it is not a constant value which may vary from
milliseconds to seconds to minutes to hours). Currently, my test RPC
programs use automatic binding method.

I am wondering how I can control the effect of the variability. Thanks for
any information and suggestion.
	-Yuh Ming


