Hi Yuh Ming,

  First of all, you will need to change your binding method since you have
no control over this time-out (or other settings) when using automatic
binding.  In general, you will need to supply the RPC binding handle to 
change default values used by the RPC runtime.

: I am wondering how I can control the effect of the variability. Thanks for
: any information and suggestion.

  There is a call, rpc_mgmt_set_com_timeout(), which you can use
to give the RPC runtime "advice" on the length of the timeout between
client and server, which also depends on the type of network protocol
that you are using.  I am enclosing the call signature, but you should
see the man pages or the DCE Application Development Reference for
the values and meanings for "timeout".  Note that these are relative
timeout suggestions to the runtime.

     void rpc_mgmt_set_com_timeout(
           rpc_binding_handle_t binding,
           unsigned32 timeout,
           unsigned32 *status);


: 	-Yuh Ming

