One of the problems about the new OSF scheme is that it makes OSF activities 
much less visible.  In August, I was told that there were 14 PSTs in progress,
only two of which had been announced publicly.

Aside from PSTs, there is a standards and architecture function that is very 
necessary.

By the way, from a DCE point of view, the new OSF business model is back to the
future.  For DCE 1.0 all of the integration work was done by a contractor (IBM).
There was only a small OSF staff involved.  The buildup of a large inhouse
development team came later.

