Digital is currently planning to support X11R6 and the Common Desktop
Environment (CDE) in the next major release which should be available
late in 1995.

CDE is based on a derivative of Motif 1.2.3. This Xm derivative has
been enhanced with a number of extensions and selected bug fixes from
Motif 1.2.4.

OSF Motif is now part of the CDE Next effort (the follow on to the CDE
1.0 release). CDE Next will be based on the OSF Motif 2.0 code base,
HOWEVER, it is already known that there will be a number of significant
modifications to Motif that will be incompatible with Motif 2.0. The
CDE Next plans have not been finalized yet, and so there may be many
more changes before we know what the next generation of Motif really
looks like.

As all of the major vendors seem to be actively supporting CDE you can
understand that OSF Motif 2.0 (in its current form) is unlikely to be
provided by any of the major vendors.

Advanced Developers Kits will be available for X11R6 and for CDE in
early 1995 with the version 3.2 release of DEC OSF/1.




