Keywords: DCE rpc public domain include

when I compiled the public domain rpc within my dce environment,
I got an error in exc_handling.c.
The problem is, that some include files are provided by the
public domain software (exc_handling.h) and some (pthread.h) are
not.
In this particular case:
- exc_handling.c includes pthread.h
- pthread.h includes cma.h and defines the type pthread_key_t later on
- cma.h includes exc_handling.h
- exc_handling.h uses extern pthread_key_t, which will be defined later
  in the body of pthread_h. 
The error did not occur before, as my old version of exc_handling.h did
not use pthread_key_t. The old exc_handling.h can not be used,
because exc_handling.c needs the new version.

The error occurred on a Unixware system and on a dec-osf1 system.

Does anybody know, how to resolve the conflict without modifying
the include files?

Wolfgang Lux
