In article <androidD05pz3.C4F@netcom.com>, <android@netcom.com> writes:
> The make fails because the
> server stub auxiliary file is not found.
 
The IDL compiler generates auxiliary files only if it needs them.  If it 
doesn't generate any, don't worry about them.  The documentation states 
that the auxiliary files will be "generated only if the interface contains 
any out-of-line, self-pointing or pipe types.  I think in fact, that the 
exact conditions are platform specific.  The basic idea is that they 
contain subroutines called by the marshalling code rather than being 
generated in line.

>The IDL compiler has an
> "saux" option (which is displayed when idl -confirm is used). But
> I can't seem to find any documentation on how to use this option.

The -saux and -caux options to idl simply allow you to specify the names of 
the auxiliary files if any.  The default names are <idlfile>_caux.c and 
<idlfile>_saux.c.

> Can anyone tell me if (a) This is the way to generate the server stub
> auxiliary file (b) where I can find documentation of all the idl compiler
> options.

The idl command and options are documented in the DCE development reference 
manual.  Your system's online documentation (man pages) may have an entry 
called "idl".

Regards,

Hal

